## Quiz Mode Standards

### Architecture
The quiz system has 6 phases: `idle → revision → asking → retrying → revealed → report`
- **idle**: Mode selection cards (Concept/Guided/Challenge), score summary, optional revision/report buttons
- **revision**: Pre-quiz last-minute review card (keyIdea, watchFor, quickTip, complexity)
- **asking/retrying/revealed**: Active question with options, feedback, per-mode features
- **report**: Post-quiz performance analysis (score, concept breakdown, weak points, advice, actions)

### Three Quiz Modes (Cadence Levels)
| Mode | Weight | Identity | Special Features |
|------|--------|----------|-----------------|
| Concept (light) | 1 only | Build understanding | Key Idea insight box after each answer, no timer |
| Guided (normal) | 1-2 | Follow the flow | Progress bar, hints on wrong, full explanations |
| Challenge (intensive) | 1-3 | Master every decision | 15s countdown timer, streak multipliers (x2 at 3+, x3 at 5+) |

### QuizQuestion Contract
- `prompt` must be answerable from the canvas/visualization alone
- `options` must NOT contain the comparison/data that decides the answer (no leaks)
- `correctIndex` is deterministically hashed from questionId for stable positioning
- Use `buildOptions(questionId, correct, distractors)` for answer assembly

### Adapter Pattern
Each category has a `quizAdapter.ts` that exports:
- `buildXxxCheckpoints(steps, algorithmKey) → QuizCheckpoint[]` — questions from step data
- `buildRevisionData(algorithmKey) → QuizRevisionData` — pre-quiz review data

Revision data must include: description, complexity (time+space), keyIdea, watchFor (2-3 items), quickTip

### Dynamic Question Generation
Use `components/quiz/quizQuestionBuilder.ts` shared utilities:
- `compareStepQuestion(step, nextStep, stepIdx)` — "Will these elements be swapped?"
- `valueAtQuestion(step, idx, label, stepIdx)` — "What value is at index X?"
- `stateTransitionQuestion(step, nextStep, field, stepIdx, label)` — "What changes?"
- `sortedCountQuestion(step, stepIdx)` — "How many are in final position?"
- `nextActionQuestion(step, nextStep, stepIdx, name)` — "What does the algorithm do next?"

Questions should derive from actual step data, NOT hard-coded prompts. The sorting adapter is the gold standard.

### Post-Quiz Report Requirements
- Score summary: X/Y correct, percentage, best streak
- Concept breakdown: grouped by concept tag, sorted worst-first
- Weak points: concepts with wrong answers + "What to review" advice
- Contextual advice based on score percentage
- Actions: Retry, Try Harder Mode (disabled if already Challenge), Back to Learning

### UI Standards
- All quiz UI lives in the `quiz-dock` slot (first card in right-hand rail)
- Use CSS variables: `--quiz-accent` (#818cf8), `--quiz-ok-soft`, `--quiz-bad-soft`
- Mode cards: icon + name + identity tagline, active card gets accent border
- Timer bar: 4px height, accent color → red when ≤5s remaining
- Progress bar: 3px height, accent color fill
- Streak badge: yellow background with Zap icon, shown when multiplier > 1
- Insight box: accent-tinted background with Lightbulb icon (Concept mode only)
- Report card: score percentage (green ≥70%, amber ≥50%, red <50%), concept bars, weak points

### Page Integration Pattern
```tsx
<QuizDock
  session={quizSession}
  cadence={cadence}
  onCadenceChange={setCadence}
  algorithmName={selectedAlgorithmName}
  onRetry={() => quizSession.resetSession()}
  onHarderMode={() => {
    const next = cadence === 'light' ? 'normal' : 'intensive';
    setCadence(next);
  }}
/>
```
Use `maskNarration(step.description, quizSession.phase)` to prevent step narration from spoiling answers.

### Testing Checklist
- [ ] Revision card shows before first question when revisionData exists
- [ ] Mode cards render with correct icons and identities
- [ ] Timer starts in Challenge mode, auto-reveals at 0
- [ ] Progress bar shows in Guided mode
- [ ] Streak multiplier badge appears at 3+ streak
- [ ] Key Idea insight box shows in Concept mode after reveal
- [ ] Report card shows after last checkpoint with score, concepts, weak points
- [ ] Retry resets session, Harder Mode bumps cadence
- [ ] Same behavior across all 14 categories
- [ ] Works in all 5 themes
